# A Note on Parallelism Effects in Processing Deep and Surface Verb-phrase Anaphora.

**Authors:** Mauner, Gail, And Others

## Abstract
Reports a reanalysis of the data on surface and deep anaphors reported by Tanenhaus and Carlson and two experiments based on the reanalysis. The parallelism effects for deep anaphors were eliminated following short passives but not full passives. The results support the claim that deep and surface anaphors access different types of representations. (25 references) (Author/CK)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ505221

